/*!
    \page vscodeext-how-build-with-cmake-presets.html
    \previouspage vscodeext-how-tos.html
    \nextpage vscodeext-reference.html

    \ingroup vscodeext-how-to-cpp
    \ingroup vscodeext-how-to-qml

    \title Build with CMake presets

    Instead of using CMake kits for building projects, you can set build options
    in a \c CMakePresets.json file. Create the presets file in the format
    described in \l{CMake: cmake-presets(7)} and store it in the project's root
    directory.

    \QVSC reads and uses all the fields that the CMake extension supports.

    \section1 Configure presets

    The following configure presets tell CMake to do a \e Debug build with the Qt
    version that you set in \c CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE:

    \badcode
    {
        "version": 3,
        "configurePresets": [
            {
                "name": "debug",
                "displayName": "my debug configure preset",
                "binaryDir": "build-debug",
                "cacheVariables": {

                    "CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE": "Debug",
                    "CMAKE_EXPORT_COMPILE_COMMANDS": "ON",
                    "CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE": "C:\Qt\6.9.1\msvc2022_64\lib\cmake\Qt6\qt.toolchain.cmake"
                }
        ]
    }
    \endcode

    The following sections describe alternative ways of using CMake presets to
    register Qt.

    \section1 CMake variables

    Instead of \c {CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE}, you can also use one of the following
    keys:

    \list
        \li \c {CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH}
        \li \c {Qt5_DIR}
        \li \c {Qt6_DIR}
        \li \c {Qt6_ROOT}
        \li \c {QT_ADDITIONAL_PACKAGES_PREFIX_PATH}
        \li \c {QT_PACKAGES_PREFIX_PATH}
        \li \c {Qt_ROOT}
        \li \c {QTDIR}
    \endlist

    \section1 CMake configure presets

    Instead of CMake keys, you can use the \c {toolchainFile} CMake configure
    preset to set the path to the toolchain file:

    \badcode
    {
        "version": 3,
        "configurePresets": [
            {
                "name": "debug",
                "displayName": "my debug configure preset",
                "binaryDir": "build-debug",
            },
            "toolchainFile": "/home/user/vcpkg/scripts/buildsystems/vcpkg.cmake"
        ]
    }
    \endcode

    \section1 Qt vendor presets

    You can also use Qt vendor presets to register the Qt installation.

    To set the path to the Qt installation, use \c {VSCODE_QT_INSTALLATION}:

    \badcode
            "vendor": {
                "qt-cpp": {
                    "VSCODE_QT_INSTALLATION": "C:\Qt\6.9.1\msvc2022_64"
                }
            }
    \endcode

    To set the path to \c qtpaths, select \c {VSCODE_QT_QTPATHS_EXE}:

    \badcode
            "vendor": {
                "qt-cpp": {
                    "VSCODE_QT_QTPATHS_EXE": "C:\Qt\6.9.1\msvc2022_64\bin\qtpaths"
                }
            }
    \endcode

    \sa {Register Qt installations}
*/
